[Music]  it's all about competition you know you  got to compete you know you got to  compete to be the best whether that's in  sports or it's in business  I'm Derek Jeter former shortstop of the  New York Yankees and now partner at  Arena Club  I played 23 professional years in  baseball and that's just a small portion  of your life you got a long life to live  afterwards so I think you have to make  sure you prepare yourself for that I  started thinking about post baseball  life Maybe  10 years prior to my retirement you know  I I've always been one that prided  myself on being prepared and I didn't  want to wake up when my playing career  was over and say what am I going to do  next my time on the field was most  important but I definitely started  thinking about what's next  my thoughts went to ownership team  ownership so what I tried to do is learn  as much as I possibly could about an  organization I lived in Florida next to  the Yankees Player Development complex  so I learned as much as I could about  Player Development scouting analytics  you know during my career made every  decision when it came to contract  negotiations marketing PR these are all  pillars of an organization biggest  lesson I wouldn't say it's any lesson  that any new lesson I've learned look  it's all about people it's all about who  you surround yourself with it's all  about having the same goals and  aspirations and work ethic so whether  you're on the field you're off the field  it's all the same you know business and  professional sports very similar  [Music]  current advice I would say is meet as  many people as you can I ask a lot of  questions and I think you learn through  experiences you learn through people  what you're passionate about when you  have that platform of playing a  professional sport one thing that you  get is access and if you have that  access I think you should meet as many  people as you can you know you play  sports you turn 30 years old people tell  you how old you are and then when you  retire you become young again so I knew  I had a long life to live after my  playing career  got three young girls right now and I  want to be present with them and their  lives I just don't necessarily think I  have the time to commit to doing what I  was doing when I was in my family I  think that's the most important I want  to be there for my girls help them find  out what they're passionate about and be  there to support them  [Music]

